+### A long span, then the sliver that matters
+Use when the second half of the lesson lives in a sliver of the first: a timeline of billions of years and the
+last ten thousand, a number line to a million and the interval from zero to one.
+Tools: `camera fit=<a>,<b>` (or `camera zoom= on=`) on a `timeline` or `numberline`, then `camera reset`. The line's
+range never changes, only the window; the ticks re-number for it.
+```
+schema timeline
+mark a event year=-4500000000 label="Earth forms"
+mark c event year=-66000000 label="dinosaurs end"
+mark d event year=-10000 label="farming"
+mark e event year=0 label="now"
+Say: "Farming and now sit on one dot: zoom |in|in to the sliver with people in it."
+@in camera fit=d,e
+Say: "And |back|back out: that is how thin it is."
+@back camera reset
+```
+
 ### Grids and tables
 Use for matrices, boards, dynamic-programming tables, truth tables: cells in rows and columns.
 Tools: `array cols=… items=[…]`; `M[r][c]`, a row `M[r][:]`, a column `M[:][c]` for `enclose`, `focus`, `indicate`.
