+## 8m. 2026-10-24: the camera on number lines and timelines
+
+**Asked.** Decision D11 from the axiom audit: a 4.5-billion-year geology timeline, then "zoom in to the last ten
+thousand years"; a number line to a million, then the interval [0, 1]. Axiom 2 forbids re-ranging the line and the
+camera, the sanctioned way to look closer, refused anything but `axes`/`plane` (camera.cpp:19). The timeline's
+ranges were `float`: ticks read `-4499999744` and the one at year 0 read `256`.
+
+**Found.** `camApply` already works in base pixels and only reads the schema's view at the top and writes it back
+at the bottom; a line is that same camera with one coordinate. Claude had written 2 camera lines in 63 real turns
+(both `camera spin`) and no timelines: the prompt said "only on `axes` and `plane`".
+
+**Built.** One camera for both: on a line the base is the line's range (y a unit range nobody uses, every thing at
+y = 0), `camPoint`/`camBox` give a thing's value on the line, the fit uses only the width (two things frame however
+close they are; one thing gets a third of the line, as on a plot), the zoom cap is 1e9 (the line maps in doubles;
+the float axes keep 1000), the view is written back into `nl_.min/max`, and both 1D layouts cull what leaves the
+window (as `layoutAxes` does; `fitStage` ignores culled things). The schema's range (`nlMin_…tlMax_`, prescan or
+`range=`) is never written by the camera, so `reset` returns to it. The follow spring now acts on the displacement
+to the goal, so a far-off centre keeps its digits. `rm::NumberLine` is `double` with a `ticks()` that uses the
+axes' dividing chain (`viz::tickLevels`: the finer step fades in, ticks are `k * step`, labels from `tickText`), used
+by the number line's `draw` and the timeline's furniture; the 1D ranges, targets and `DataCtx` are `double`.
+No new syntax. README's camera section, chat/prompt.md and the toolbox (a new move, "A long span, then the sliver
+that matters") say so; `scripts/geology.dan` is the regression script.
+
+**Measured.** Tests: four new engine cases (number-line fit with the far thing culled and `range=` untouched;
+timeline zoom-on plus reset; follow on a number line; the exact range and tick labels), all failing on the old
+engine. `make test`, `make check` (125 ok + toolbox 28 ok), `make golden` 0 WORSE, `make append` as before
+(space-downhill / space-saddle). Frames: the geology zoom at 1, 6.5, 7.5 and end, the number line at 1 and end.
+
+**Not done.** The tick numbers of number lines and timelines are still not in the layout checker (they were not
+before); the 2D axes' ranges stay `float`; no thousands separators on big tick numbers ("-4500000000").
