+# The camera on a timeline: four and a half billion years, then the sliver with people in it.
+# The line's range never changes (axiom 2); the window does, and comes back.
+title "Earth's history, then the last ten thousand years"
+schema timeline
+mark a event year=-4500000000 label="Earth forms"
+mark b event year=-3800000000 label="first life"
+mark c event year=-66000000 label="dinosaurs end"
+mark d event year=-10000 label="farming"
+mark e event year=0 label="now"
+Say: "The whole of Earth's history on one line: farming and now sit on top of each other."
+Say: "Zoom |in|in to the sliver with people in it."
+@in camera fit=d,e
+Say: "From the first farms to today, the line is all ours."
+Say: "And |back|back out, to see how thin that sliver is."
+@back camera reset
